**The thesis:** Wang built a $29B company by industrializing other people's judgment, then got hired into a job where the judgment has to be his own. The hook and ending both hang on one line from the Theo Von interview — a sixth-grade math competition where the top four in New Mexico won a Disney World trip, and his own account of it: *"I got fourth place, so I snuck in there."* LeCun's January attack lands on exactly that nerve.

**Bespoke section:** "Scoring Alexandr Wang the way Scale AI scores a model" — a benchmark card with a third column for what the score can't see. Scale's real business is model evals, so the form comes from his own company and collapses if transplanted.

